D["B2_CAND_CHAR_ADANNA_TURNAROUND_BACK_V003_2560x1440.png"] = "Four-view turnaround sheet, plate 3 of 4, titled ADANNA TURNAROUND BACK. The main panel shows a full back view on light grey: braids in a high knot, indigo bandeau, diagonal leather strap, indigo wrap skirt, bronze armlet on the viewer-left arm, and leather sandals. The sidebar lists seven corrections, locks checked and open qualifications. The labels read EXPLORATORY, NOT APPROVED CANON, STATUS REVIEW REQUIRED, UNAPPROVED, PENDING REVIEW, and the footer says the sheet supersedes V002 and depicts no blade."
D["B2_CAND_CHAR_ADANNA_TURNAROUND_FRONT_V003_2560x1440.png"] = "Four-view turnaround sheet, plate 1 of 4, titled ADANNA TURNAROUND FRONT, labelled V003. The main panel shows a full front view on light grey: braids in a high knot, indigo bandeau, a leather diagonal strap, a bronze armlet, an indigo wrap skirt tied at the left side, and sandals. The sidebar lists corrections, locks and open qualifications. Labels read EXPLORATORY, NOT APPROVED CANON, REVIEW REQUIRED, UNAPPROVED, PENDING REVIEW."
D["B2_CAND_CHAR_ADANNA_TURNAROUND_FRONT_V004_2560x1440.png"] = "Same front turnaround layout, labelled V004, plate 1 of 4, marked EXPLORATORY NOT APPROVED CANON and STATUS REVIEW REQUIRED. The figure on light grey wears braids in a high knot, an indigo bandeau, a leather diagonal strap, a pendant on a cord at the neck, a bronze armlet, an indigo wrap skirt and sandals. The sidebar lists nine corrections, and the footer says V004 supersedes V003 and that only the pendant cord and the three-quarter arm were touched."
D["B2_CAND_CHAR_ADANNA_TURNAROUND_LEFT_SIDE_V003_2560x1440.png"] = "Four-view turnaround sheet, plate 2 of 4, titled ADANNA TURNAROUND LEFT SIDE, labelled V003. The main panel shows a full left profile on light grey: braids in a knot, an indigo top, a bronze armlet on the upper arm, a leather strap across the shoulder, an indigo wrap skirt and sandals. Labels read EXPLORATORY NOT APPROVED CANON and STATUS REVIEW REQUIRED."
D["B2_CAND_CHAR_ADANNA_TURNAROUND_THREE_QUARTER_V003_2560x1440.png"] = "Four-view turnaround sheet, plate 4 of 4, titled ADANNA TURNAROUND THREE QUARTER, labelled V003. The main panel shows a three-quarter view turned toward the figure's right on light grey: braids in a high knot, an indigo top, a leather diagonal strap, a bronze armlet on the upper arm, an indigo wrap skirt with a tie, and sandals. Labels read EXPLORATORY NOT APPROVED CANON and REVIEW REQUIRED."
D["B2_CAND_CHAR_ADANNA_TURNAROUND_THREE_QUARTER_V004_2560x1440.png"] = "Same three-quarter turnaround layout, labelled V004, plate 4 of 4. The figure on light grey wears braids, an indigo top, a leather diagonal strap, a pendant on a cord, a bronze armlet, an indigo wrap skirt and sandals. The footer says V004 supersedes V003 and that only the pendant cord and the three-quarter arm were touched. Status: EXPLORATORY NOT APPROVED CANON, REVIEW REQUIRED."
D["B2_CAND_SCENE_CH01-SCN-006_A_LARGE_FAMILY_COMPOUND_V002_1672x941.jpg"] = "Photograph-style view of a mud-walled compound. A wooden gate stands open in a red mud wall, thatched round huts sit beyond it, indigo cloth and hanging pots and gourds are on the wall at left, a mortar and pestle and a woodpile sit under a thatched shelter at right, and a woven mat with grain and a round tray lie on red earth. Footer: SCENE_CH01-SCN-006 A LARGE FAMILY COMPOUND V002, EXPLORATORY NOT APPROVED CANON, STATUS REVIEW REQUIRED, figures 0."
D["B2_CAND_SCENE_CH01-SCN-010_SMITHY_V002_1672x941.jpg"] = "Interior view of an open-sided smithy at sunset. A clay hearth holds glowing embers, two hand bellows lie beside it, a wooden block serves as an anvil, tongs and a hammer lie on the ground, metal blanks sit on a bed of ash, and clay storage pots stand at right. Village huts are visible through the open side. Footer: SCENE_CH01-SCN-010 SMITHY V002, EXPLORATORY NOT APPROVED CANON, REVIEW REQUIRED, figures 0."
D["B2_CAND_SCENE_CH01-SCN-012_MARKET_STALLS_V002_1672x941.jpg"] = "Elevated view of a village market at sunset. Raised stalls with thatch and woven mats hold produce laid out on mats and tables, including green peppers, yams, bananas, red fruit in bowls and gourds. Clay pots stand on a stand at right, cloth lies folded on a bench at left, and mud walls and palms sit behind. Footer: SCENE_CH01-SCN-012 MARKET STALLS V002, EXPLORATORY NOT APPROVED CANON, REVIEW REQUIRED, figures 0."
D["B2_CAND_SCENE_CH01-SCN-017_VILLAGE_SQUARE_V002_1672x941.jpg"] = "Open dirt square at dusk between mud-walled round houses with conical thatched roofs and crenellated wall tops. A large tree at upper right shades a wooden bench, and a mortar, pestle and two clay pots sit at lower right. Hazy sky and more houses show in the distance. Footer: SCENE_CH01-SCN-017 VILLAGE SQUARE V002, EXPLORATORY NOT APPROVED CANON, REVIEW REQUIRED, figures 0."
D["B2_CAND_SCENE_CH01-SCN-022_STREETS_V002_1672x941.jpg"] = "Narrow lane between mud walls. One side has a thatched eave and a wooden door frame, a palm-pole and thatch canopy runs overhead, a clay pot and a mortar stand at the foot of a pole, and gourds and a light cloth hang from a line on the right wall. Footer: SCENE_CH01-SCN-022 STREETS V002, EXPLORATORY NOT APPROVED CANON, REVIEW REQUIRED, figures 0."
D["B2_CAND_SCENE_CH01-SCN-032_WELLS_V002_1672x941.jpg"] = "Two stone-lined circular wells in a muddy yard, with a rope and a gourd dipper at the rim of one well. A goat stands at left by thatched huts, a shallow drainage channel with grass runs across the yard, a woodpile and a mortar sit at right, and a broken clay pot lies in the foreground. Footer: SCENE_CH01-SCN-032 WELLS V002, EXPLORATORY NOT APPROVED CANON, REVIEW REQUIRED, figures 0."
D["B2_CAND_SCENE_CH01-SCN-033_GATES_V002_1672x941.jpg"] = "Wooden gate frame of two upright posts and a cross beam, tied with cord, set into brushwood-topped mud walls. Beyond it a dirt path leads between thatched round huts and trees under an overcast sky. Footer: SCENE_CH01-SCN-033 GATES V002, EXPLORATORY NOT APPROVED CANON, REVIEW REQUIRED, figures 0."
D["B2_CAND_SCENE_CH01-SCN-034_ROADS_V002_1672x941.jpg"] = "Dirt lane between tall red mud walls with thatched roofs above. Two blue cloth door hangings sit in doorways on the right-hand wall, a wet track with footprints and debris runs down the middle, sparse grass grows at the wall bases, and thatched huts and trees stand beyond. Footer: SCENE_CH01-SCN-034 ROADS V002, EXPLORATORY NOT APPROVED CANON, REVIEW REQUIRED, figures 0."
D["B2_CAND_VR-011_LANDING_OF_UNCLAIMED_V002_2560x1440.png"] = "Wide view of a grey mud shore. Many dark dugout canoes are drawn up in rows, and a foreground canoe holds wrapped bundles, pots and folded cloth with a paddle laid across it. A tall dark rampart runs along the right side with pale cloth strips hanging from poles on its top, and still water and low hills lie at left. The sidebar reads REGISTER CH07-SUB-004, scene CH07-SCN-011, PROPOSED."
D["B2_COMPARE_ADANNA_TURNAROUND_V002_alignment.jpg"] = "Alignment sheet headed ADANNA TURNAROUND V002. Four views sit in a row on grey panels (front, left side, back, three quarter), each with crown, floor and height values printed below. Text reads height spread 4 px, crown spread 0 px, floor spread 4 px. It states the baldric runs over her right shoulder to her left hip in all four plates, that the armlet and temple beads stay on her anatomical left, and that the blade and scabbard are omitted. It is marked as a candidate, not an approved asset."
D["B2_COMPARE_ADANNA_TURNAROUND_V003_alignment.jpg"] = "Alignment sheet headed ADANNA TURNAROUND V003, with four panels numbered 1 front, 2 left side, 3 back and 4 three quarter, on light grey. Each panel has crown, floor and height values. Text reads height spread 4 px, crown spread 0 px, floor spread 4 px, and that the baldric runs from her anatomical left shoulder to her right hip. It also says V002 was rejected on seven points, and marks the status EXPLORATORY NOT APPROVED CANON, UNAPPROVED PENDING REVIEW."
D["B2_COMPARE_COSTUME_BREAKDOWN_V001_vs_V002.jpg"] = "Two-panel costume breakdown comparison. The left panel is CHAR_ADANNA_COSTUME_BREAKDOWN_V001, marked UNAPPROVED PENDING CD, with a front figure annotated for scar on left cheek, spiral pendant, indigo wrap top, leather strap and stud, and hip-scabbard position, plus right-side, back and lower-body panels labelled UNRESOLVED. The right panel is the V002 candidate, marked UNAPPROVED PENDING CD, with identity locks, a tag key, a front and three-quarter figure, and hatched unresolved areas for the right side, back torso and lower body with weapon. Text below lists rejection points and the method."
D["B2_COMPARE_ESTABLISHING.jpg"] = "Side-by-side comparison headed ESTABLISHING VIEW ENV_LAST_DAUGHTER_ANCESTRAL_REALM_ESTABLISHING, V005 to V006. The left panel is the V005 master: mud houses with thatched roofs, a long open-sided hall on pillars at left, a stepped mound of houses at right, and a hazy warm sky. The right panel is the V006 candidate with the mound rebuilt. Sheet text says the highest master in the drive is V005, that a small figure was removed by hand, and that the candidate is review required."
D["B2_COMPARE_ESTABLISHING_V005_vs_V007.jpg"] = "Base and candidate panels of the ancestral realm establishing view. The base V005 shows a regular stepped mound at right, and the candidate V007 shows a masked rebuild with an irregular mass of houses on the mound. Lower crops show the mound and the mound foot where it meets the foreground. Sheet text gives 441,432 px total changed, 365,251 px inside the mask, lists defects A to E, and marks the status CANDIDATE ONLY, REVIEW REQUIRED."
D["B2_COMPARE_ESTABLISHING_V005_vs_V008.jpg"] = "Base V005 and candidate V008 establishing views. The candidate shows the mound rebuilt at village scale, made of many small houses with ladders and stair runs, and a fine aerial river that thins at the mound's flank. Lower crops show the mound and the river detail. Sheet text gives 406,016 px total changed, 332,417 px inside the mask, lists defects 2a to 2c and 3, notes requirement D not delivered, and marks CANDIDATE ONLY, REVIEW REQUIRED."
D["B2_COMPARE_ESTABLISHING_V008_vs_V009.jpg"] = "Sheet comparing V008 and V009 of the establishing view. The top panels show full views with side text blocks. Section A shows the mound foot, where a hard seam is softened into drifting dust. Section B shows the lower-right mist veil corrected warmer. Section C shows the right compound, where a cramped longhouse becomes an open yard with a small thatched house and a staked plot. Section D is a 2x crop of the staked house. Sheet text lists the option A ruling and five defects."
D["B2_COMPARE_ESTABLISHING_V009_vs_V010.jpg"] = "Sheet comparing V009 and V010 of the establishing view. The top panels show full views. Section A shows the hill dwellings, which are smaller and roughly doubled in number, with the same outline. Section B shows the hill foot against the plain village. Section C shows the right compound, unchanged between the two versions. Section D is a 2x crop of the hill houses. Sheet text says the change is a single authorised correction and marks review required."
D["B2_COMPARE_ESTABLISHING_V010_vs_V011_CHROME.jpg"] = "Sheet of text panels and two thumbnails. The panels show a CLIENT REVIEW BLOCK for V010 with a stale round label, a V011 entry marked PENDING with no client ruling recorded, a footer panel with the exploratory disclaimer and a colour swatch #DCC3AA, and a V011 version register entry. The lower line reads panel pixels 0 changed (verified), chrome 8,046 px. The two thumbnails at top compare V010 and V011."
D["B2_COMPARE_ESTABLISHING_V011_vs_V012.jpg"] = "Sheet comparing V011 and V012 of the establishing view. The top panels show full views. Section A shows the yard with the cloth line and paling. Section B shows the wall behind the paling with a generative patch. Section C shows the lower-right wall with the pale blue cast corrected to warm earth. Section D is a 2x crop of the cloth line. Sheet text lists items 2 and 3 and notes that item 1 (house scale) was not attempted."
D["B2_COMPARE_ESTABLISHING_V012_vs_V013.jpg"] = "Diagnostic comparison of V012 and V013 of the establishing view. Section A shows the frame margin and lower-right wall, with the margin and wall colours given as printed values. Section B shows the cloth line at the right end: V012 has a hard cut seam and a pale wedge, and V013 shows the cloth re-rendered as fabric. Section C shows Nneka's House, which is about 15 percent smaller in V013 with the striped side cloth restored. Sheet text states that the basal hill huts were not re-proportioned."
D["B2_COMPARE_VR-008.jpg"] = "Sheet headed VR-008 COMP_ADANNA_SEALED_QUARTER_HAND_ON_SEAL, V005 to V006. The left panel is the V005 master: a woman with a silver shoulder piece and a dark-blue top stands in a mud alley with her right hand on a plaster panel with a crack, beside a bowl and a pot. The right panel is the V006 candidate with the same frame and a more prominent crack. Sheet text states a hand retouch on the panel only, zero pixels changed outside the panel box, and that the crack is now more prominent."
D["B2_COMPARE_VR-008_V005_to_V008_with_references.jpg"] = "Sheet headed VR-008 COMP_ADANNA_SEALED_QUARTER_HAND_ON_SEAL, V005 base to V008 candidate. Two full-frame images show a woman with her hand on a sealed plaster door in a mud alley, with V008 as the candidate. Below are crops of the midriff (V004 reference and V008 restored), the armlet (CHAR master portrait, V007 painted and V008 transferred) and the fracture (V005 and V008). Footer text lists defects A to D, 12,194 px changed, and status CANDIDATE ONLY, REVIEW REQUIRED."
D["B2_COMPARE_VR-008_V005_vs_V007.jpg"] = "Before and after panels headed VR-008, V005 to V007. Both show the same woman with her hand on a sealed door in a mud alley. Below are three crops: the midriff (V005 and V007), the left upper arm armlet (V005 and V007, with painted coiled bands in V007), and the fracture (V005 and V007). Text reads 13,618 changed pixels, all inside three masks, and status CANDIDATE ONLY, REVIEW REQUIRED."
D["B2_COMPARE_VR-008_V008_vs_V009.jpg"] = "Composition sheet pair titled VR-008 SEALED QUARTER, V008 to V009. The top shows full composition panels with side text blocks. Section A shows the left shoulder: V008 has a metal pauldron and V009 has bare shoulder with a plain leather strap. Section B shows the coiled bronze armlet in both versions, unchanged. Section C shows a crop of the sheet chrome. Footer text says the environment is untouched."
D["B2_COMPARE_VR-010.jpg"] = "Two-panel comparison headed VR-010 ENV_HOME_SETTLEMENT_WASHING_PLACE, V002 to V003. The left panel is the V002 master: a clay pot and jar, a flat stone washing slab, a woven screen, and a bright wet runoff channel crossing open ground. The right panel is the V003 candidate, where the channel ends in a stone-lined culvert at the foot of the compound wall and the yard is unbroken earth. Sheet text notes slight drift in the screen weave and the background trees."
D["B2_COMPARE_VR-010_WASHING_PLACE_V002_vs_V004.jpg"] = "Sheet headed WASHING PLACE, V002 base to V004 candidate. Two full frames show a washing corner with a woven screen, a clay pot and jar, a flat stone slab, a leaf, chewing sticks and a sponge. The V004 frame shows no runoff channel. Crops show the runoff channel before and after and the slab, pots and splash earth. Sheet text gives 113,314 px changed, all inside the repaint corridor, and marks the status CANDIDATE ONLY, REVIEW REQUIRED."
D["B2_COMPARE_VR-010_WASHING_PLACE_V002_vs_V005.jpg"] = "Sheet headed WASHING PLACE, V002 base to V005 candidate. Two full frames show the washing corner, with the V005 frame showing flush ground, a woven screen corner, a pot, a slab, a soap leaf and chewing sticks, and no visible drain. Crops show the flush ground, the slab with pot, and the woven screen. Captions read HOME SETTLEMENT and status CANDIDATE ONLY, REVIEW REQUIRED."
D["B2_COMPARE_VR-011.jpg"] = "Two-panel comparison headed VR-011 ENV_GATES_DEAD_LANDING_OF_UNCLAIMED, V001 master to V002 candidate. The left panel shows dark canoes on a mud shore with bundles and folded cloth, and cloth strips on the rampart poles that read as small flags. The right panel shows the strips hanging straight and a denser canoe field, with darker, calmer water. Sheet text lists three defects, and says the chapter 7 status is still PROPOSED, not canon."
D["B2_COMPARE_WALL_OF_HOUSES.jpg"] = "Two-panel comparison headed WALL OF HOUSES, ENV_LAST_DAUGHTER_ANCESTRAL_REALM_WALL_OF_HOUSES, V003 master to V004 candidate. Both show a foggy mound of mud-brick houses with thatched roofs stacked up a slope. The V004 candidate has a bluer, paler fog and two pale plastered doorway panels at the foot of the mound. Sheet text lists defects A to C and residual notes."
D["B2_COMPARE_WALL_OF_HOUSES_V003_vs_V005.jpg"] = "Sheet headed WALL OF HOUSES, V003 base to V005 candidate. Two full frames show a mud-brick mound of houses in mist. The candidate has a thatched house with a sealed doorway at the foot of the mound, and a doorway-states strip shows lit, dark and plain-sealed doorways. Sheet text lists defects A, C, D and F, gives 1,234,163 px total changed, and marks the status CANDIDATE ONLY, REVIEW REQUIRED."
D["B2_PIXELDIFF_VR-008_V007.jpg"] = "Dark pixel-difference map of the VR-008 V005 panel to the V007 panel. A dim copy of the woman and alley is shown with three green boxes: A fracture 1,504 px, B midriff 8,481 px, and C armlet 3,633 px, each with a white changed-pixel mask. Text gives 13,618 changed pixels of 2,222,269 total, all inside the three masks, and lists chrome edits separately."
D["B2_RETOUCH_GUIDE_VR-006_BLOCKED.jpg"] = "Composition sheet titled ADANNA IN THE MOTHERS' COURTYARD. A rendered scene shows a woman with a scabbard beside a tree, a loom, jars, a broom and a mortar in a mud courtyard. Callouts mark point A at her left hip (KEEP) and point B at the current tip, with a target line and an action note to shorten the sheath. Side text gives status REQUIRES REVISION and a scabbard check. The filename contains BLOCKED; the picture itself is fully readable."
D["B2_RETOUCH_GUIDE_VR-007_BLOCKED.jpg"] = "Composition sheet titled ADANNA INSIDE NNEKA'S HOUSE. A seated woman on a sleeping platform by an open doorway holds a sheathed weapon, with a mat, jars, a basket and a hearth nearby. Callouts mark point A at the spiral pommel (KEEP) and point B at the chape disc (MOVE UP), with a target line for the tip and a current lowest-point line. Side text includes a recurring-fault note. The filename contains BLOCKED; the picture itself is fully readable."
D["CAND_ESTABLISHING_V013_2560x1440.png"] = "Establishing view sheet, ENV_LAST_DAUGHTER_ANCESTRAL_REALM_ESTABLISHING V013, status review required. The scene shows a long hall on pillars at left, a stepped mound of houses with ladders at right, mud houses with thatched roofs in the middle, and a yard with a cloth line and stakes at lower right. The sidebar lists changed items and items not fixed. The footer reads EXPLORATORY NOT APPROVED CANON, with versions V005 base and V006 to V012 kept."
